---
description: Prefer common code names over raw code values in UI
alwaysApply: true
---

# Common Code Display Rule

## Goal
- In user-facing UI, display `name` from common-code APIs instead of raw `code` values.

## Required Practice
- If a status/type/category has a common-code group, map `code -> name` before rendering text or badges.
- Keep raw `code` only as a fallback when common-code lookup fails.
- Avoid exposing backend/internal code strings (e.g. `PENDING`, `PO_CLOSED`, `REGISTERED`) to general users by default.

## Implementation Notes
- Reuse `getCommonCodesByGroup` and project constants in `src/api/commonCode.ts`.
- Prefer a small helper per screen (e.g. `displayNameForStatus(code)`).
- If this mapping is repeated in many screens, extract a shared utility/hook.

## Example
```tsx
const { data: statusCodes = [] } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ["commonCodes", COMMON_CODE_GROUP_DELIVERY_STATUS],
  queryFn: () => getCommonCodesByGroup(COMMON_CODE_GROUP_DELIVERY_STATUS, accessToken!),
});

const statusLabel = (code?: string | null) =>
  statusCodes.find((item) => item.code === String(code ?? "").trim())?.name ||
  code ||
  "-";
```
